  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Temple University (Temple or TU) is Philadelphia’s only public university in Pennsylvania, United States. The university has 17 schools and colleges, including 5 professional schools, offering over 640 academic programs.</p><p>Temple is ranked among the top 100 national universities and the top 50 public schools by the U.S. News &amp; World Report (2025). The University is also ranked R1 for research under the Carnegie Classification, indicating the high level of research activity among four-year universities.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>At TU, you’ll be among students from over 120 nationalities on campus. With a student-faculty ratio of 12:1, you’ll be part of an interactive and inclusive learning environment with personalised teaching.</p><p>Not only that, Temple University offers a vibrant campus life with over 100 student organisations and clubs catering to a wide array of interests. It also provides state-of-the-art recreational facilities for you to stay active and engaged. The Campus Recreation Centre includes gyms, weight rooms, and cardio areas. And then there’s the Aramark STAR Complex climbing wall, an outdoor track, and many more facilities.</p><p>There are also intramural sports leagues and club sports teams that you can participate in, such as basketball, soccer, and many more.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>Temple University provides on-campus housing for first-year students. Transfer student housing options are also available, on a first-come, first-served basis.</p><p>Temple’s residence halls offer a variety of living spaces across its 6 on-campus residence halls, including apartment-style to double and single rooms. It also provides accessible housing for students with disabilities.</p><p>Additionally, if you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, <a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\">download our app</a> and check out the Stays feature!</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Library</strong><br>Temple University’s Charles Library offers state-of-the-art resources and learning spaces, multipurpose rooms, and a cafe. The Loretta C. Duckworth Scholars Studio within the library is a creative space for digital research and projects, offering you tools for 3D printing, virtual reality, and much more.</p><p><strong>Sports</strong><br>At Temple, you can choose to join over 30 sports clubs and several varsity athletic teams, 18 of which compete at the Division 1 level. These include the sports teams in basketball, cross country, football, golf, soccer, tennis, field hockey, gymnastics, rowing, track and field, and volleyball.</p><p><strong>Laboratory</strong><br>TU houses state-of-the-art laboratories that support research and hands-on learning. Key lab facilities include the Innovation Lab and Engineering Research Laboratories, the Science Education and Research Centre (SERC), the Health Sciences Labs, and many more.</p><p><strong>Cafeteria</strong><br>TU offers a variety of cafe options. At Morgan Hall North, you’ll find the largest dining hall on campus with popular eateries. The most popular places to eat at the campus include the Esposito Dining Centre at Johnson and Hardwick Halls, and the Howard Gittis Student Centre Food Court, among many others.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
